    "Day 1 Morning Summary:\n",
    "\n",
    "I learned how to use Pandas to read a CSV file into a DataFrame.\n",
    "\n",
    "I can use head() and info() to check data structure and missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "I know how to calculate the mean() and std() for numeric columns.\n",
    "\n",
    "Using groupby('Tool_ID'), I found that Tool_B has a higher average defect count (19.5) and a larger standard deviation (2.12) compared to Tool_A (mean 12.0, std 1.0). This indicates Tool_B might have a stability issue, but we need more data like Recipe ID and Wafer counts to confirm if it's a real excursion."
